## 🔍 Feature Importance

Random Forest feature importance is used to identify which transaction features contribute most to fraud classification.

Logistic Regression coefficients are also analyzed to understand the relative influence of the features on the prediction.

---

## ⚖️ Precision vs Recall in Fraud Detection

In fraud detection, **Recall is particularly important** because failing to identify a fraudulent transaction can result in financial loss.

However, maximizing Recall alone can produce more false positives.

Therefore, an effective fraud detection system should find an appropriate balance between:

**Precision ↔ Recall**

The F1-Score and PR-AUC provide additional ways to evaluate this balance.

---

## 🚀 Scalability

A real-world financial system may need to process millions of transactions per hour.

For a system handling approximately **1 million transactions per hour**, the trained model could be deployed as a real-time prediction service.

Possible improvements include:

* Real-time streaming data processing
* Model deployment through an API
* Distributed processing using technologies such as Apache Spark
* Automated feature engineering
* Model monitoring
* Data drift detection
* Threshold optimization
* Periodic model retraining

The model would be trained offline and then used to make fast predictions on incoming transactions.

