---

## 💡 Key Insights

* The dataset is **extremely imbalanced**, with fraudulent transactions representing only a small fraction of all transactions.
* Accuracy alone is not sufficient for evaluating fraud detection models.
* SMOTE helps address class imbalance during model training.
* Recall is an important metric because undetected fraud can result in financial loss.
* Precision is also important because excessive false alerts can inconvenience legitimate customers.
* Random Forest provides feature importance that helps understand influential transaction characteristics.
* PR-AUC is particularly useful when evaluating highly imbalanced classification problems.

